Subject: [PATCH] feat: comment likes + reply counts (item A.6, frontend half)

Adds a heart-toggle like button with count next to every comment, and
shows the reply count directly on the Reply button (e.g. 'Reply (3)')
- reply counts needed no backend change since replies were already
stored as an array, so the count is just their length.

Like state fetched in one bulk request alongside the existing car
like-status fetch, using the new comments/likes/me endpoint - not one
request per comment. Liking updates optimistically (toggles the UI
immediately) and reverts only if the request actually fails, guarded
against double-clicks with a busy flag.

Backend endpoints (already committed separately):
POST /cars/{car_id}/comments/{comment_id}/like
GET /cars/{car_id}/comments/likes/me?comment_ids=a,b,c
